    "text": "<p>During which of the following processes, does entropy decrease ?</p><p>(A) Freezing of water to ice at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math><br />(B) Freezing of water to ice at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math><br />(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />(D) Adsorption of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and lead surface<br />(E) Dissolution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> in water</p>",
